<title>POLAND: Olawa, Remak resume trade Tues.</title>
<headline>Olawa, Remak resume trade Tues.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish non-ferrous metals smelter Olawa SA and engineering firm Remak SA will resume trade on the Warsaw bourse's main market on Tuesday after Monday's one-day suspension, the bourse said.</p>
<p>On Monday those two companies and cement firm Gorazdze, paintmaker Polifarb Wroclaw and chemical firm Viscoplast were suspended due to the threat to them caused by flooding in southern Poland.</p>
<p>The latter three firms along with electrode maker ZEW and industrial boilermaker Rafako remain suspended due to the floods. ZEW and Rafako were suspended since late last week.</p>
<p>Both Olawa and Remak said in statements earlier on Monday that the flooding in the region had caused them no problems.</p>
<p>Water currently covers thousands of square kilometeres of southern Poland and police estimate the death toll of the week-old catastrophe at 36.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
